  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 254 PM EDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nBeginning the long term on Thursday, the troughing will be \nelongated over the eastern CONUS with a push of vorticity moving \ninto the area throughout the day as the front is over the north \nGeorgia area. Current guidance suggests stalling over the I-85 \ncorridor for Thursday. As a result rain chances are in the likely \nrange as showers and thunderstorms are expected during the \nafternoon and evening hours. Current soundings show that storms \nshould stay subsevere but will need to watch for any flooding \nconcerns with very little shear in the area when these storms \nform. With high PWATs in the 1.8-2\" range and the storms expected \nto form along the flow this could also increase our flooding \nthreat. WPC has placed the area in a slight ERO as well. Pushing \ninto Friday, expecting similar conditions with the trough still \nfully over our area. Saturday will begin the pattern change with \nshowers and thunderstorms mostly over the southern half of the \narea and ridging beginning to build in over the central and \neastern CONUS. As a result rain chances begin to decrease Sunday \ninto Tuesday with only 20-30% chances during the afternoon. \nTemperatures will be seasonable in the mid 80s to low 90s across \nthe area through Saturday before beginning to warm slightly into \nthe mid 90s as riding begins settling in Saturday and Sunday.",
